Assign Plans and Set User Overrides

Question

We are extending Feature Entitlements to let administrators assign subscription plans to users and grant or revoke feature overrides for individual users.
This lets the platform team move customers between tiers and lets support teams unblock or restrict a specific feature for one customer without changing their overall plan.

Add two functions to the FeatureService class:

2-1) assign_plan

The assign_plan function takes a user_id and a plan, and assigns that plan to the user, following these rules:

The plan must already exist.
Assigning a plan to a user who already has one replaces the previous assignment.
Return true if the assignment succeeds. Return false if the plan does not exist.

2-2) set_user_override

The set_user_override function takes a user_id, a feature name, and an enabled boolean value. It should add or update a feature override for that user, following these rules:

The user must already have an assigned plan.
The feature must be defined in at least one subscription plan, though not necessarily the user's own plan.
The enabled value is always a boolean and may explicitly enable or disable the feature.
If the user already has an override for the feature, replace it.
Return true if the override is added or updated. Return false if the user has no assigned plan, or if the feature is not defined in any plan.

