Recommend Minimal Plans

Question

Because per-feature overrides now carry a significant surcharge, the sales team wants plan recommendations for a list of customers so accounts can be moved to whichever plan saves them the most money.

Add one function to the FeatureService class. You may reuse any function already in the class.

4-1) recommend_plans

The recommend_plans function takes a list of user_ids and returns a list of recommendations, following these rules:

For each user, find the plan that costs the least while matching their exact current access - either a plan whose defaults already cover everything they have, or a cheaper plan with some paid overrides added.

A user's "effective entitlements" are all features the user currently has access to, applying overrides over plan defaults exactly as has_feature does.

Consider every feature that appears in any plan's defaults or in the user's overrides.

The cost of a plan for a user, while matching their effective entitlements exactly, is calculated the same way as calculate_monthly_charge in the previous question.

best_plan is the plan with the lowest such cost, and best_cost is that cost. If two plans tie on cost, choose the one with the higher base tier.

Skip user_ids that have no assigned plan. If a user_id appears more than once, include it once.

Return one entry per user as a dictionary with the keys "user_id", "best_plan", and "best_cost", sorted by user_id ascending.

Do not modify any stored data.

